commit e0508cf2aa88bdd908a10844b0687519b1bc79b4
Author: Toti Gonzales <dntstudios101@yahoo.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 3 16:59:53 2026 +0200

    feat(shaders): Fog, waterfall spray, clouds and smoke (experimental)
    
    On top of the lava, water, ice and tar shaders:
    
    - the fog block (unconnected purple pane): drifting mist, traced through
      its block
    - the spray block (unconnected light blue pane): waterfall mist, thin
      curling strands, grainy as the mist texture, its grains streaming
      every way
    - clouds and smoke as whole volumes, one block each, which the vertex
      shader spreads over the screen and the fragment shader traces once
      per pixel (fog_volume.glsl): a cloud (grey pane); a 40-wide smoke
      column, one light grey pane every 16 blocks up it, magenta on top;
      chimney smoke (brown pane)
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

